[32m+[m[32m# MedSTT: Architecture and Capability Document[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Purpose of this document:** a technical, factual account of what MedSTT is,[m
[32m+[m[32mhow it works, what it has been verified to do, and what its current, honest[m
[32m+[m[32mlimitations are. This document is written for government technical review. It[m
[32m+[m[32mdoes not minimize open items or unresolved risks — every limitation named here[m
[32m+[m[32mis a real, current state of the system, not a hypothetical edge case.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. What MedSTT Does[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMedSTT converts audio recordings of clinician-patient conversations into[m
[32m+[m[32mstructured clinical documentation: a nurse intake record (vitals, prior test[m
[32m+[m[32mresults) and a doctor's prescription record (problem summary, symptoms,[m
[32m+[m[32mmedications, advice, follow-up), with a generated PDF as the final clinical[m
[32m+[m[32martifact. It is designed around a three-role model — admin, nurse, doctor —[m
[32m+[m[32mmatching how a real clinical encounter proceeds.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**The system does not make clinical decisions.** Every AI-generated output —[m
[32m+[m[32mtranscripts, extracted entities, drafted intake data, drafted prescriptions —[m
[32m+[m[32mis explicitly a draft requiring human review before it becomes part of the[m
[32m+[m[32mclinical record. This is not a design aspiration; it is enforced at multiple[m
[32m+[m[32mlevels described in Section 3.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. System Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.1 High-level pipeline[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA clinical encounter produces one or two audio recordings (a nurse vitals-[m
[32m+[m[32mtaking session and/or a doctor consultation), which move through the following[m
[32m+[m[32mstages:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Ingestion** — upload or live browser recording, validated (real file[m
[32m+[m[32m   properties inspected via ffprobe, not trusted from client-supplied metadata)[m
[32m+[m[32m   and normalized to a standard 16kHz mono WAV format.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Chunking** — voice activity detection (Silero VAD) and speaker[m
[32m+[m[32m   diarization (pyannote.audio) segment the recording into speaker-labeled,[m
[32m+[m[32m   appropriately-sized chunks.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Transcription** — each chunk is transcribed by a local, GPU-resident[m
[32m+[m[32m   speech-to-text model (Google's MedASR), run concurrently with a cloud[m
[32m+[m[32m   fallback (Azure AI Speech) for cross-verification.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Quality assessment** — each transcript is scored using the model's own[m
[32m+[m[32m   real per-token confidence (not a heuristic proxy), combined with pattern-[m
[32m+[m[32m   based checks (repetition, speech-rate anomalies) and cross-checked against[m
[32m+[m[32m   the cloud transcription for agreement.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Human-in-the-loop (HITL) flagging** — any transcript failing quality or[m
[32m+[m[32m   consensus checks is routed to a review queue rather than silently accepted.[m
[32m+[m[32m6. **Entity extraction** — validated transcripts are processed by clinical[m
[32m+[m[32m   named-entity-recognition models (disease and medication/chemical entities),[m
[32m+[m[32m   each extraction independently confidence-scored and validated.[m
[32m+[m[32m7. **Drafting** — a local large language model (Google's MedGemma) drafts[m
[32m+[m[32m   structured clinical content from the validated transcripts and entities:[m
[32m+[m[32m   vitals/test extraction for nurse intake, and problem/symptoms/medications/[m
[32m+[m[32m   advice/follow-up for the doctor's prescription.[m
[32m+[m[32m8. **Human review and finalization** — a doctor reviews and edits the drafted[m
[32m+[m[32m   prescription; a nurse reviews and edits the intake form. Only after explicit[m
[32m+[m[32m   finalization does either become part of the permanent record. A PDF is[m
[32m+[m[32m   generated at finalization, with an explicit AI-provenance disclosure printed[m
[32m+[m[32m   on the document itself.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.2 Technology stack[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Layer | Technology | Notes |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Backend | FastAPI, async SQLAlchemy, Alembic | Python 3.12 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Frontend | React, Vite, TypeScript | Role-based routing and access control |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Database | PostgreSQL 16 | UUID primary keys, append-only audit log, row-versioning for AI-generated content |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cache/sessions | Redis 7 | Server-side sessions (not JWT) for instant revocation |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Local speech-to-text | google/medasr (105M param Conformer) | GPU-resident, CUDA required |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Cloud speech-to-text | Azure AI Speech | Runs concurrently with local ASR for cross-verification |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Speaker diarization | pyannote.audio 4.0.7 | CPU-only in this deployment |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Voice activity detection | Silero VAD | CPU-only |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Clinical entity extraction | OpenMed NER models (PharmaDetect, DiseaseDetect, 434M params each) | CPU-only |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Clinical text generation | google/medgemma-1.5-4b-it | GPU-resident, CUDA required, ~8GB VRAM |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Observability | Prometheus metrics, structured JSON logging, cross-request tracing | |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Containerization | Docker, Docker Compose | GPU passthrough via NVIDIA Container Toolkit |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2.3 GPU resource management[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe local speech-to-text model (MedASR) and the local text-generation model[m
[32m+[m[32m(MedGemma) both require CUDA and cannot both be resident in GPU memory[m
[32m+[m[32msimultaneously on an 8GB card — MedGemma alone was measured using approximately[m
[32m+[m[32m6.2GB of the card's 8GB capacity in isolation. A dedicated model orchestrator[m
[32m+[m[32menforces strict mutual exclusion: only one model is ever loaded at a time, with[m
[32m+[m[32man explicit lock preventing race conditions during concurrent requests, and[m
[32m+[m[32mexplicit memory cleanup on every model swap. This is a hard architectural[m
[32m+[m[32mconstraint of the current deployment, not an optimization choice — it directly[m
[32m+[m[32mdetermines that the production deployment runs as a single backend worker[m
[32m+[m[32mprocess (see Section 5).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Safety and Human Oversight Design[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis system was built around a consistent principle: AI-generated content is[m
[32m+[m[32mnever presented as, or silently converted into, an authoritative clinical[m
[32m+[m[32mrecord without human review. This is enforced structurally, not just through[m
[32m+[m[32mpolicy:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Every AI-generated database record carries explicit provenance fields**[m
[32m+[m[32m  (which model produced it, what version, the complete raw output) that[m
[32m+[m[32m  persist even after a human edits the record. The original AI output is never[m
[32m+[m[32m  silently overwritten or lost.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Prescriptions and intake forms cannot be finalized by the system itself.**[m
[32m+[m[32m  They are created in a draft state and require an explicit action by the[m
[32m+[m[32m  responsible role (doctor for prescriptions, nurse for intake forms) to[m
[32m+[m[32m  finalize. Editing a finalized record is rejected by the system.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The final PDF document itself carries an explicit AI-provenance[m
[32m+[m[32m  disclosure** whenever any part of its content was AI-drafted, stating the[m
[32m+[m[32m  model used and that the content was reviewed and approved by the named[m
[32m+[m[32m  clinician and requires independent verification. This is not only an[m
[32m+[m[32m  internal database flag — it is visible on the physical/printed clinical[m
[32m+[m[32m  artifact.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A dedicated human-in-the-loop review queue** captures any transcript that[m
[32m+[m[32m  fails quality checks (low model confidence, detected repetition, anomalous[m
[32m+[m[32m  speech rate) or disagrees materially with the independent cloud[m
[32m+[m[32m  transcription, routing these to an administrator for review rather than[m
[32m+[m[32m  silently accepting uncertain content into the pipeline.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Both underlying AI models' own publishers state explicitly that their[m
[32m+[m[32m  outputs require independent clinical verification and are not intended to[m
[32m+[m[32m  directly inform diagnosis or treatment decisions.** This system's entire[m
[32m+[m[32m  review-and-finalize architecture exists specifically to honor that[m
[32m+[m[32m  requirement, not as an incidental feature.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3.1 A concrete example of this design working as intended[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDuring development, a real quality issue was identified and corrected: an[m
[32m+[m[32mearly version of the vitals-extraction logic misidentified a spoken phrase[m
[32m+[m[32mdescribing bowel movement frequency ("six or seven times a day") as a pulse[m
[32m+[m[32mrate reading. This was caught through structured testing against real[m
[32m+[m[32mrecordings before the feature was used in any live capacity, and the[m
[32m+[m[32mextraction logic was rebuilt to require the model to cite the exact source[m
[32m+[m[32msentence supporting any extracted value — creating a verifiable link a human[m
[32m+[m[32mreviewer can check, rather than trusting an unverifiable number. This is[m
[32m+[m[32mrepresentative of the broader development approach: every AI integration in[m
[32m+[m[32mthis system was tested against real audio and real transcripts before being[m
[32m+[m[32mconsidered complete, and issues found in that testing were treated as design[m
[32m+[m[32mproblems requiring a structural fix, not tuned away with a quick patch.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Data Handling and Security[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Authentication**: server-side sessions (Redis-backed), enabling instant[m
[32m+[m[32m  revocation of access — an administrator deactivating a compromised or[m
[32m+[m[32m  departing user's account takes effect immediately, not upon token expiry.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Password storage**: Argon2id (current OWASP recommendation), with account[m
[32m+[m[32m  lockout after repeated failed attempts and rate limiting on the login[m
[32m+[m[32m  endpoint as a separate, complementary protection against broader abuse.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Role-based access control**: every endpoint enforces role requirements[m
[32m+[m[32m  (admin/nurse/doctor) at the API layer.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Audit logging**: every significant action (logins, record creation,[m
[32m+[m[32m  edits, status changes, HITL resolutions, prescription finalization) is[m
[32m+[m[32m  written to an append-only audit log with no update or delete capability.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Data integrity**: UUID primary keys (record existence/count is not[m
[32m+[m[32m  inferable from sequential IDs), soft-deletion of clinical records (never[m
[32m+[m[32m  destructive deletion), and row-versioning for AI-generated content[m
[32m+[m[32m  (original and human-corrected versions both preserved, never overwritten).[m
[32m+[m[32m- **File handling**: uploaded audio and generated PDFs are stored using[m
[32m+[m[32m  randomly-generated filenames, never the original filename or any[m
[32m+[m[32m  patient-identifying string, reducing the risk of PHI exposure through[m
[32m+[m[32m  filesystem-level access independent of database access controls.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A dedicated security hardening review** was performed covering CORS[m
[32m+[m[32m  configuration, cookie security, secrets management, input validation, and[m
[32m+[m[32m  request size limits. This review found and corrected two real gaps: a[m
[32m+[m[32m  missing global request-size limit on JSON endpoints, and a `.gitignore`[m
[32m+[m[32m  omission that could have allowed PDF files containing real patient names and[m
[32m+[m[32m  clinical data to be committed to version control (confirmed, via direct[m
[32m+[m[32m  inspection of repository history, that this had not yet actually occurred[m
[32m+[m[32m  before the fix was applied).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**What this system does not yet provide**, stated plainly: HTTPS/TLS[m
[32m+[m[32mtermination (must be provided by infrastructure fronting this system in any[m
[32m+[m[32mreal deployment); FIPS 140-2/3 compliance (would require replacing the current[m
[32m+[m[32mpassword hashing algorithm if formally required); and an automated database[m
[32m+[m[32mbackup strategy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Known Limitations[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis system has real, current limitations. They are listed here directly[m
[32m+[m[32mbecause an accurate account of what is not yet solved is more useful to a[m
[32m+[m[32mtechnical reviewer than a document that omits them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **No background task queue.** Several pipeline stages (chunking,[m
[32m+[m[32m   transcription, entity extraction, AI-assisted drafting) are long-running[m
[32m+[m[32m   synchronous operations — the text-generation step alone has been measured[m
[32m+[m[32m   taking 80 to 258 seconds depending on the task. Under concurrent real-world[m
[32m+[m[32m   load, this is the single most significant scalability constraint of the[m
[32m+[m[32m   current system.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Single backend process, by design.** The GPU resource management[m
[32m+[m[32m   approach described in Section 2.3 requires this; scaling beyond one[m
[32m+[m[32m   process would require a different GPU-sharing architecture.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **The speaker diarization library is running a different version than[m
[32m+[m[32m   originally intended** (a newer release pulled in during development,[m
[32m+[m[32m   rather than the specific version originally pinned to avoid a known[m
[32m+[m[32m   resource-usage issue in GPU contexts). This has not caused an observed[m
[32m+[m[32m   problem in the current CPU-only diarization configuration, but remains an[m
[32m+[m[32m   open item to formally resolve.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **The AI-assisted nurse intake extraction path is implemented but has not[m
[32m+[m[32m   been tested against a real two-recording clinical encounter** (one[m
[32m+[m[32m   recording for vitals-taking, one for the doctor consultation) — only the[m
[32m+[m[32m   manual-entry intake path has complete, real-world verification. This[m
[32m+[m[32m   reflects the genuine sequencing of development, not a hidden gap.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **This system has been deployed and verified in one environment**[m
[32m+[m[32m   (a local development machine running Docker with GPU passthrough). It has[m
[32m+[m[32m   not yet been tested on a separate, independent server or cloud[m
[32m+[m[32m   infrastructure. A first deployment to new infrastructure should be treated[m
[32m+[m[32m   as a real validation exercise, not an assumed repeat of prior testing.[m
